<%# A step of the creation of a character (CharacterCreationSteps), in the frame of the creation
    (layouts/character_creation): only this area scrolls, under the centered title of the step; the buttons stay in
    their bar at the bottom (_actions, sticky). Then the fields of the sections of this step, laid out by type like a
    sheet of a game (CharacterSheets::FieldsHelper), or the summary. The values worked out from the others follow what
    the player types (character_sheet_controller.js), and the server works them out the same way (@computed_sheet_values).
    relative: a box hidden in a card (sr-only, absolute) stays in this area, never past it %>
<div class="relative flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-y-auto">
  <div class="@container flex min-h-full flex-1 flex-col px-4 pt-6 sm:px-8">
    <%= render "game_tables/character_steps/title", title: character_step_label(@step), lede: @step.intro %>
    <% if @step.summary? %>
      <%= render "character_sheets/summary/sheet", character: @character %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render "game_tables/character_steps/step_form", character: @character, step: @step,
                                                          computed: @computed_sheet_values %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
